From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 15:04:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: fix LPI enhanced mgmt TX on narrow channels

When lpi_bcn_enhance is set, every fixed-rate 6 GHz management frame
is forced to 80 MHz bandwidth so beacons keep their range under LPI
PSD power limits. The override also applies to probe requests sent
from scan and ROC dwells, where the radio is tuned to a 20 MHz
channel; the hardware cannot honor the forced bandwidth there and
most of these frames never make it on air (TX status reports an
error). Hidden-SSID 6 GHz APs then never hear our directed probes,
so a backhaul STA cannot rediscover its AP after the AP reboots or
changes channel: scans keep showing the BSSID from beacons while the
SSID never resolves, until a rare probe transmission succeeds.

Apply the override only while the current chandef is at least 80 MHz
wide. This keeps the enhancement on AP operating channels (beacons,
probe responses, on-channel management frames) and restores normal
management TX during scans. Fix both the mt7996 and connac2
(mt7915/mt7986) copies of the logic.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 mt76_connac_mac.c |    8 +++++++-
 mt7996/mac.c      |    8 +++++++-
 2 files changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/mt76_connac_mac.c
+++ b/mt76_connac_mac.c
@@ -611,9 +611,15 @@ void mt76_connac2_mac_write_txwi(struct
 							vif ? &vif->bss_conf : NULL,
 							beacon, multicast);
 		u32 val = MT_TXD6_FIXED_BW;
+		/* 80 MHz mgmt TX is only possible while the radio is on a
+		 * chandef of at least that width; during scan/ROC dwells the
+		 * phy sits on a 20 MHz channel and the forced bandwidth makes
+		 * most frames (e.g. probe requests) fail to transmit.
+		 */
 		if (dev->phys[band_idx]->cap.has_6ghz &&
 			dev->phys[band_idx]->lpi_bcn_enhance &&
-			ieee80211_is_mgmt(hdr->frame_control))
+			ieee80211_is_mgmt(hdr->frame_control) &&
+			cfg80211_chandef_get_width(&dev->phys[band_idx]->chandef) >= 80)
 			val |= MT_TX_BW_IDX_80;
 		/* hardware won't add HTC for mgmt/ctrl frame */
 		txwi[2] |= cpu_to_le32(MT_TXD2_HTC_VLD);
--- a/mt7996/mac.c
+++ b/mt7996/mac.c
@@ -921,9 +921,15 @@ void mt7996_mac_write_txwi(struct mt7996
 
 		if (mcast)
 			val |= MT_TXD6_DIS_MAT;
+		/* 80 MHz mgmt TX is only possible while the radio is on a
+		 * chandef of at least that width; during scan/ROC dwells the
+		 * phy sits on a 20 MHz channel and the forced bandwidth makes
+		 * most frames (e.g. probe requests) fail to transmit.
+		 */
 		if (dev->mt76.phys[band_idx]->cap.has_6ghz &&
 		    dev->mt76.phys[band_idx]->lpi_bcn_enhance &&
-		    ieee80211_is_mgmt(hdr->frame_control))
+		    ieee80211_is_mgmt(hdr->frame_control) &&
+		    cfg80211_chandef_get_width(&dev->mt76.phys[band_idx]->chandef) >= 80)
 			val |= FIELD_PREP(MT_TXD6_BW, FW_CDBW_80MHZ);
 		txwi[6] |= cpu_to_le32(val);
 		txwi[3] |= cpu_to_le32(MT_TXD3_BA_DISABLE);
